A meteorologist in Indianapolis, DavidLetterman, is run out of town for warning ofhail "the size of canned hams." You believehim and take cover for two hours.Caroler Carol is a famous figure in Chicago.Every Christmas she goes to the Chicago Zooand sings carols to the animals. The penguinsseem to love it as much as the newspapers.20Harry wants Chicago deep-dish pizza for a snack.Getting the pizza is no problem since it'sserved all over town, but you spend two hours trying to find a "pizza-ever-hot" box.Indiana is named "the Hoosier State" after thebrown, furry rodents that live predominantlyin the lower portion of the state. This animal,the hoosier, is Indiana University's mascot.20"When in Rome, do as the Romans do." You goout for Friday Fish Fry in Wisconsin but don't remember the way back from the countryinn that fried the fish. Lose three hours.Chicago is called "the Windy City" because itis the gustiest city in the world. Gales offLake Michigan sometimes reach 150 mph.30You fall in love with the Minneapolis sound -the Replacements, Prince, and Soul Asylum.So many bands, so little time. Harry tellsyou just how little: you've wasted an hour!The Metrodome, home of the Minnesota Twins,is called "the Homerdome" because it has areputation for being an easy field in whichto hit home runs.11The Polar Bear Club offers you membership.You learn too late that the main activityis a New Year's Day dip in Lake Michigan.Spend two hours thawing out.Detroit's auto giants, despite slumping inthe 1980s, have rebounded and today supplythree-quarters of the nation's cars.21You spend two hours dancing the polka atthe Bratskeller in Madison; you spend athird hour giving Harry a song and danceabout how it's all part of your research.Smelting, a popular activity in Wisconsin,involves the use of metal detectors to locatethe smelt metal underground. Residents searchfor this metal on the sands of Lake Michigan.30You enjoy a ride on the "el," downtownChicago's elevated rail system, but losetwo hours when you mistakenly take the"A" train instead of the "B" train.The Little 500 is a bike race held everysummer at Ohio State University in Columbus.20You visit Sears Tower, the world's tallestbuilding, to see four states and hopefullyUncle Bernie's house (you promised mom to"see" him while in Illinois). Lose 2 hours.The Twin Cities are included in the AmericanExpress "Top 10 Places in the World toVisit."21You visit the John Dillinger Historic Museumto see the gory artifacts of his criminalcareer, and spend one hour hiding in thestairwell.Cincinnati has been called the "Queen Cityof the West," "Porkopolis," and "America'smost beautiful inland city."20You get lost in the largest student union inthe world. When Hoosier boosters start tofollow, you make a run for it. Lose twohours, but escape Hoosier conversion.Wisconsin is known as "the Badger State" and"America's Dairyland." Tin miners earnedthe first nickname by their burrowinginto the hills of the state's southwest.21